 from Claude Opus 4.7 .\nL92: \nL93: \nL94: Fast mode is not available on Claude Opus 4.6. Requests to `claude-opus-4-6` with `speed: \"fast\"` do not return an error: they run at standard speed and are billed at cite84†standard rates rather than fast mode's premium rates, and the response reports cite85†`usage.speed: \"standard\"` . To continue using fast mode, see cite86†Migrating to Claude Opus 5.5 from Claude Opus 4.6 and earlier Opus models .\nL152: The response `usage` object includes a `speed` field that indicates which speed was used, either `\"fast\"` or `\"standard\"`. Requesting `speed: \"fast\"` on a cite91†model that doesn't support fast mode returns an error, and so does exceeding fast mode's rate limits or capacity (a `429` or `529`). When a request with `speed: \"fast\"` succeeds, `usage.speed` is `\"fast\"`. If you are using Claude Opus 4.6 and request fast mode, its behavior is unique.\nL153: Instead of returning an error like other models that don't support fast mode, it silently switches to standard speed. Though there is no error with Opus 4.6, the `speed` field accurately shows `\"standard\"`.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nComputation and Language Feb 2026 (https://arxiv.org/list/cs.CL/2026-02?show=100&skip=400)\nciteturn31566view8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn31565view4\",\"pattern\":\"Title:\"}); Total lines: 933\nL80: Title: Investigating the structure of emotions by analyzing similarity and association of emotion words\nL81: \nL82: cite78†Fumitaka Iwaki , cite79†Tatsuji Takahashi L83: \nL84: Comments: 5 figures, 8 tables; data github link added\nL85: \nL86: Subjects: Computation and Language (cs.CL); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL87: \nL88: [409] cite80†arXiv:2602.06440 [cite81†pdf , cite82†html , cite83†other ]\nL89: \nL90: \nL91: Title: TrailBlazer: History-Guided Reinforcement Learning 